// ne_glyph_tro.go — the trees away from full resolution (docs/ne-glyph.md §Trees far out).
// With the trees on and no crown sheet to show (full resolution off, or all of LOD 2) the map carries one green sheet: a hexagon per H3 cell of the observed-layer
// peer's stand index, greener = taller trees, fuller = more of them (the canopy sheet's ramp, so nothing jumps where that takes over) — res 7 for Austria, res 8 / 9 / 10
// for a box small enough (ne_tree_stands.go, /api/v1/ne/glyph/trees). A quiet chip in the
// map's corner counts the trees in view.
package main

// neGlyphTroCSS — the sheet and the corner chip (the chip wears the height scale's glass).
